<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραληπ-τέον</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλαμβάνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must
				take to oneself</i>, [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκα</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Antip.Stoic.
				3.257
			</span></i> ; <i>one must provide oneself with</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάρτυρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					34.30
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one must apply</i> remedies, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.519
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.29.15
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τοῦ λύχνου φέγγος
			π</span>. Herod.
				Med.
			in<i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				58.71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ληπτέος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <i>to be
			applied</i> or <i>employed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὁ κλυστήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					80
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἁλτῆρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Gym.</u>
					55
				</span></i>
			.</div>
